The trigonometry calls a deterministic implementation (this package's port/)

Detour's hooks dtMathCosf, dtMathSinf and dtMathAtan2f forward to the
platform's C library, and Recast's rcMarkWalkableTriangles and
rcClearUnwalkableTriangles call cosf for the walkable slope; the C libraries'
results differ by an ulp between glibc, macOS libSystem, the Windows UCRT and
emscripten's musl. This package promises the same mesh, path and crowd step on
every platform, so the three hooks and Recast's two calls use
port/DeterministicMath.cpp (IEEE arithmetic in double, one rounding to float,
within 1 ulp of the correctly rounded result; tests/trig_test.cpp). sqrtf,
floorf, ceilf and fabsf stay: IEEE makes them exact everywhere.
Wrapper-specific (the port is this package's), not for upstream.

Apply from upstream/recastnavigation: git apply -p1 ../../patches/0002-deterministic-math-hooks.patch

diff --git a/Detour/Include/DetourMath.h b/Detour/Include/DetourMath.h
index 5528ead..b02e8ca 100644
--- a/Detour/Include/DetourMath.h
+++ b/Detour/Include/DetourMath.h
@@ -8,14 +8,15 @@ Members in this module are wrappers around the standard math library
 #define DETOURMATH_H
 
 #include <math.h>
+#include "DeterministicMath.h"
 
 inline float dtMathFabsf(float x) { return fabsf(x); }
 inline float dtMathSqrtf(float x) { return sqrtf(x); }
 inline float dtMathFloorf(float x) { return floorf(x); }
 inline float dtMathCeilf(float x) { return ceilf(x); }
-inline float dtMathCosf(float x) { return cosf(x); }
-inline float dtMathSinf(float x) { return sinf(x); }
-inline float dtMathAtan2f(float y, float x) { return atan2f(y, x); }
+inline float dtMathCosf(float x) { return mcpplibs::mwrap::recastnavigation::port::cosf(x); }
+inline float dtMathSinf(float x) { return mcpplibs::mwrap::recastnavigation::port::sinf(x); }
+inline float dtMathAtan2f(float y, float x) { return mcpplibs::mwrap::recastnavigation::port::atan2f(y, x); }
 inline bool dtMathIsfinite(float x) { return isfinite(x); }
 
 #endif
